<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-course-navigation">
  <title>Course Navigation</title>

  <p>
    To ensure you are seeing all resources and progressing through the course as intended,
    use a web browser on a computer whenever possible. Some Canvas features do not display
    well in the mobile app. Chrome is recommended.
  </p>

  <paragraphs>
    <title>Course Homepage</title>
    <p>
      Use the Canvas course homepage as your main starting point. From that page, you can
      access weekly overviews, lesson materials, support resources, Ask a Peer | Help a Peer,
      and writing assignments.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs>
    <title>Weekly Announcements</title>
    <p>
      Weekly announcements include important course updates and guidance on what to do next.
      Configure your Canvas notifications so you receive announcements promptly.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs>
    <title>Modules and Requirements</title>
    <p>
      Move through the course using the weekly announcements or the course homepage, then the
      next buttons at the bottom of each page. Complete each module requirement in order to
      unlock later lessons and assessments.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <p>
    If you are unable to access a lesson because of prerequisites, complete the listed items
    in the earlier module first. If you run into trouble, contact your instructor right away.
  </p>
</section>
